Chapter: TcoBitopLoop
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A self tail recursive loop whose tail-call argument is a bit operation
 must terminate and answer. On RISC-V these hung: the frameless tail
 call lowered two of its three argument paths with the general emitter,
 which uses a0 and a1, and in a frameless function a0 and a1 ARE the
 parameters, so the loop lost its induction variable and spun forever.
 The cross harness recorded that as a test producing no output at all.

 Each loop below selects a different branch of the frameless two-
 argument tail call, chosen by whether each argument reads the OTHER
 parameter. loop-both takes the both-read path, which was always
 correct; loop-a0 and loop-none took the two paths that were not. The
 three-parameter loop is the control: over two parameters the frameless
 path is not taken at all, so it answered throughout.

 These pass on x86-64 whether or not the backend is right, so this file
 earns its place in the cross battery rather than the default one. Keep
 the arithmetic loops beside the bit ones: an immediate-eligible
 argument lowers by a different route and stayed correct, which is what
 made the bit operations the suspect.

Section: Bit Operations In Tail Position

  loop-both : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-both (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-both (bit-and k 255) (acc + 1)

  loop-a0 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-a0 (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-a0 (bit-and k 255) (k + 1)

  loop-none : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-none (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-none (bit-and acc 255) (k + 1)

  loop-shru : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-shru (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-shru (bit-shru acc 1) (k + 1)

  loop-shl : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-shl (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-shl (bit-shl acc 1) (k + 1)

  loop-xor : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-xor (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-xor (bit-xor acc 1) (k + 1)

  loop-or : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-or (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-or (bit-or acc 1) (k + 1)

  loop-shr : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-shr (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-shr (bit-shr acc 1) (k + 1)

  loop-not : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-not (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-not (bit-not acc) (k + 1)

  loop-mod : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-mod (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-mod (int-mod acc 1000) (k + 1)

Section: Controls

  loop-sub : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-sub (acc) (k) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-sub (acc - 1) (k + 1)

  loop-and3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  loop-and3 (acc) (k) (pad) =
   if k >= 8 then acc
   else loop-and3 (bit-and acc 255) (k + 1) pad

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("loop-both: " & show (loop-both 0 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-a0: " & show (loop-a0 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-none: " & show (loop-none 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-shru: " & show (loop-shru 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-shl: " & show (loop-shl 1 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-xor: " & show (loop-xor 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-or: " & show (loop-or 254 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-shr: " & show (loop-shr 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-not: " & show (loop-not 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-mod: " & show (loop-mod 123456 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-sub: " & show (loop-sub 255 0))
    print-line-uni ("loop-and3: " & show (loop-and3 255 0 7))
  end
